The scroll listener is probably mutating a `@Published` property on every frame, causing the entire view tree to re-render. Fix:

```swift
// ❌ Bad — triggers full re-render
class DashboardVM: ObservableObject {
    @Published var scrollOffset: CGFloat = 0  // fires every frame
}

// ✅ Good — isolate the scroll state
// Option A: Use @State directly on the view (not ObservableObject)
@State private var scrollOffset: CGFloat = 0

// Option B: If must use VM, use Combine with throttle
$scrollOffset
    .throttle(for: .milliseconds(16), scheduler: RunLoop.main, latest: true)
    .assign(to: &$throttledOffset)
```

The rule: never put high-frequency scroll values into `@Published`. Keep them in `@State` on the view that owns the scroll, or throttle them.

